## Context and authority

Filed from replicator 0002 after the author requested consolidation before numerical confirmation. Related to tracker 1552 and closed scope ticket 1561. This is a request for receiving-project Imagine, not an implementation authorization or an assertion that the existing whole-paper categories are false.

## Observation

At IDH main e6521eeca366035930ce4a0e281bda0ec53220ab, references/assessment.md lines 84-114 require whole-paper provision, while lines 122-124 already permit main-result CRA/CRR. Lines 194-220 give the derived table whole-paper coverage. A host-author override was needed to assess provision for a declared selected claim. Scoped Fully must not silently satisfy an existing whole-paper criterion.

Replicator's reviewed Arechar audit (e4cb874de0a034fbe7a97fa5b35569c4dd3fad1f) selects numerical Figures 5a/5d before dependency inspection. Their actual producer/consumer chain excludes national WVS distributions needed by supplementary Figure S4. Reassessment (a167acb57a39cb70590ef8ba066fbe990f308e8f) finds analysis input information and numerical code complete for that target, upstream raw/cleaning unknown. The broader 3/4 pilot remains unchanged. No scientific program was run and no new accuracy claim is made.

The existing primary route is ACRe Assessment, https://bitss.github.io/ACRE/assessment.html : introduction permits selected claims, display items or estimates; section 3.2 maps each item to inputs; 3.3.1 grades individual items; 3.3.3 treats paper-level practices separately. Brodeur pre-Games slides 4/9 emphasize main results/models without defining every provision category.

## Request for receiver Imagine

Represent a declared claim/output/estimate scope explicitly and propagate it through provision, execution and reference comparison. Retain a labeled whole-paper audit. Consider main-claim default for Games as a proposal; do not silently change the canonical CIRED grid, existing scope decisions, tolerances, adaptation conventions or old observations. Resolve how selected-target results coexist with existing whole-paper criteria before implementation.

Receiver owns fact/framing checks, duplicate and work-in-flight checks, ownership, standing rulings and disposition. Source preflight found only tracker 1552 open; closed 1561 deliberately established current whole-paper scope. Preserve the already merged 1565/1566 evidence fixes; these are not being refiled.

## Proposed acceptance questions

- [ ] Declared target is inspectable and consistently named at every stage; whole-paper mode remains available.
- [ ] A gap outside the target cannot become a selected-result gap; unknown required coverage stays unknown.
- [ ] Cross-scope categories cannot produce an unqualified agreement score; printed reference categories and narrative inferences stay distinguishable.
- [ ] Numerical estimates and literal rendering, information provision and software readiness, remain distinct.
- [ ] Existing grid meanings and old evidence are preserved or explicitly migrated under an approved decision.

## Evidence and handoff boundary

Assigned source project: `~/CNRS/projets/actifs/replicator`. Read reviewed reports with git show on the hashes above: replications/arechar-mainclaim-audit-2026-11-26/REPORT.md and replications/arechar-reevaluation-2026-11-26/REPORT.md. The consolidation branch t0002-consolidation carries doc/examples/arechar-mainclaim/README.md and IDH-SCOPE-BRIEF.md; its final commit will be logged after consolidation. These are references, not files to change from IDH.

No IDH skill, scientific source, comparator or canonical grid is changed by this ticket. Replicator owns downstream input/comparator follow-up. Main-claim CRA can proceed from adequate analytic inputs without resolving the upstream raw boundary first; CRR and raw-completeness claims cannot.


## Receiving Imagine (2026-11-26)

Disposition: **ACCEPTED for bounded planning**, on the author's instruction
"Réception". Land this request into the ticket store, keeping 1567 and tracker
1552 open. This is not adoption of a new default, a grid migration, or a skill
implementation. The five proposed acceptance questions remain unchanged.

1. **Facts versus framing.** Current `assessment.md:84-124,194-240` confirms
   whole-paper provision/table rows alongside selected-main-result run criteria.
   This is an explicit local contract, not a parser bug. The primary ACRe guide
   (https://bitss.github.io/ACRE/assessment.html, checked 2026-11-26, introduction
   and sections 3.1,3.2,3.3.1,3.3.3) permits selected display items or estimates,
   maps their inputs, and separates paper-level practices. It supports a
   selected-target mode; it does not prescribe our Games default or redefine
   every provision row. Brodeur slides4/9 support main-results/model emphasis,
   without settling the proposed default.

   Read pinned replicator `verification.json` and `dependencies.json` at
   e4cb874, `comparison.json` at a167acb, and the consolidated reference at
   fd85bcc. The inspected dependency graph excludes national WVS from numerical
   5a/5d and includes it for S4. Its recorded positive controls identify a
   missing required CSV/field, the off-target DTA loader, and S4's WVS gap.
   This is source-inspection evidence, not independent numerical reproduction
   or a certificate of historical package identity. The reference comparison
   contains one conditional printed-Fully entailment and one narrative-based
   inference; neither supplies a four-row accuracy score. Current work in
   replicator may advance separately from these pinned observations.

2. **Duplicates and overlap.** Open/closed ticket search, assessment history,
   open forge PRs, and worktree inventory found no competing implementation.
   Closed1561 deliberately established whole-paper scope;1565/1566 fixed
   evidence semantics.1567 asks how to represent an additional declared target
   without making scoped Fully satisfy those whole-paper criteria. It does
   not reopen their implementation or authorize rescoring old dossiers.
   PR2516 is unrelated memory capture and is preserved.

3. **Ownership.** IDH owns the skill's target declaration, vocabulary and
   propagation through its instructions. Replicator owns source retrieval,
   comparator encoding, experiments and validation there. Acceptance grants
   no authority to edit that project's scientific files from IDH.

4. **Standing decisions and next boundary.** Preserve whole-paper mode, the
   existing grid and1565/1566 unknown/gap/run distinctions. A separately named
   selected-target result can be designed without silently weakening a
   whole-paper criterion. Plan must make that coexistence explicit before
   implementation. A switch to main-claim-by-default for Games remains a
   proposal for an explicit author decision, not an ACRe mandate or a decision
   made by this ticket receipt. No tolerance, adaptation convention, prior
   observation or numerical-versus-rendering target changes at reception.

Validation of this receipt: documentary checks above; ticket format/corpus
and bookkeeping candidate checks before landing. No package was executed,
no frozen source/dossier was written, and no new assessment was produced.
